course: dictionary
lesson: 3241
title: Envoys: messengers with a mission
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An envoy is a person sent by a government or a ruler to take a message to another country, or to talk for them. Envoys carry messages and make deals, so they are important people.
explain: Read the context to find the meaning. «Real diplomacy used letters, gifts, envoys and royal marriages» tells you envoys were one way countries dealt with each other. Ask yourself: who would be sent to carry a message for a king? An envoy.
explain: A special envoy is sent to deal with one problem, such as peace talks. The brackets in «a papal envoy (a messenger of the Pope)» explain the word for you. Swap messenger into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: An envoy is a messenger sent by a government or a ruler.
fact: A special envoy is sent to deal with one problem, such as peace talks.
fact: «Volodymyr heard envoys of Islam, Judaism and Western and Byzantine Christianity», so rulers received envoys from many different faiths.
fact: «Prince Danylo of Halych received a royal crown from a papal envoy (a messenger of the Pope) in 1253.»
fact: Phrases you may meet are «special envoy», «peace envoy» and «UN envoy».
exercise: What is an envoy? | A type of ship used for fishing | *A person sent to take a message or talk for a government or ruler | A long letter written by a child | A royal crown worn at feasts
exercise: In «a papal envoy (a messenger of the Pope)», what do the brackets tell you? | That the year was 1253 | *That an envoy is a messenger | That the crown was made of gold | That the Pope is a king
exercise: What is a special envoy sent to do? | Sing at a royal wedding | Count the sheep in the fields | Cook dinner for the king | *Deal with one problem, such as peace talks
test: Which phrase is about making peace between countries? | *peace envoy | royal crown | river envoy | papal crown
test: According to «Real diplomacy used letters, gifts, envoys and royal marriages», which was a way countries dealt with each other? | *Sending envoys | Hiding their gold | Playing football | Building sandcastles
exam: Which sentence uses envoy correctly? | The envoy was a sunny afternoon at the beach. | The envoy was a big red bus parked outside. | *The king sent an envoy to the neighbouring country with a message of peace. | The envoy grew tall in the garden every summer.
